        "title": "chapters/01/probabilities.py",
        "code": "import math\n\ndef probabilities(logits, temperature=1.0):\n    peak = max(logits)\n    weights = [math.exp((x - peak) / temperature)\n               for x in logits]\n    total = sum(weights)\n    return [w / total for w in weights]",
        "sparkLine": "Exponentiate. Normalize. Return probabilities.",
        "codeSize": 0.052,
        "sparkSize": 26
      },
      "intent": "The probabilities() function as an Onda-style code card in the Claude cream skin. Spark line names the mechanism."
    },
